Package: pbs-zabbix
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, zabbix-agent2 | zabbix-agent
Description: Zabbix monitoring for Proxmox Backup Server
 Monitors Proxmox Backup Server (PBS) datastores and alerts when a scheduled
 backup did not complete successfully.
 .
 Uses Zabbix low-level discovery to enumerate every VM/CT that has ever been
 backed up (read directly from /var/log/proxmox-backup/tasks, no PBS API
 calls or root privileges required) and exposes, per VM/CT:
  - age of the last successful (TASK OK) backup, in seconds
  - the last recorded task status, for alert context
 .
 Pair the age item with a Zabbix trigger (e.g. using the
 {$PBS.BACKUP.MAXAGE} macro, with per-VMID context overrides for
 less-frequent backup schedules) to get notified as soon as a backup job
 fails or simply never ran — for example because the network path between
 the hypervisor and the PBS datastore was down.
